That is only when you are confused.

Look a bit higher up, and you'll find out that when it's merely
*blessed*, then all cursed items in your inventory become uncursed. If
it's *uncursed*, then all cursed items that you are wearing or
wielding become uncursed.

In other words: If the scroll is blessed, it will affect your entire
inventory. If it is uncursed, it will affect your worn/wielded
equipment. (Whether you are confused or not.)

     If you are not confused, it will affect cursed items, uncursing
them (whether it is blessed or uncursed: although how *many* items it
affects depends on whether it is blessed or uncursed.) If you are
confused, it will affect uncursed items, giving them a 25/50/25%
chance of becoming blessed/uncursed/confused (again, if it is blessed
or uncursed, affects only how *many* items are AFFECTED.)

In other words, you have to read a blessed scroll of remove curse
*while confused* to give all your UNCURSED items a 25% chance of
becoming blessed and a 25% chance of becoming cursed. You cannot curse
an item with a scroll of remove curse unless you are confused.

